---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy | Nimbuy" description="What personal data Nimbuy collects, why, who processes it, how long it is kept, and how to access, correct or delete it.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;font-size:0.9rem">Last updated 2 October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose legal">
        <p>This describes what the Nimbuy website does with personal data. It matches how the site works today and changes when the site does.</p>

        <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>Nimbuy, run by {SITE.founder}, decides why and how your data is used. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Nimbuy is independent and not affiliated with Amazon Web Services.</p>

        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The free check runs in your browser. The listing text you paste is <strong>never sent to us and never stored</strong>.</li>
          <li>We collect personal data only when you type it into the brief form or book a call.</li>
          <li>No advertising trackers, no analytics cookies, no selling of personal data.</li>
          <li>You can ask to see, correct or delete your data at any time.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>When</th><th>What we receive</th><th>Why, and the legal basis</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td data-label="When">You send a brief</td>
              <td data-label="What we receive">Name, work email, company, listing URL, your message</td>
              <td data-label="Why">To reply, scope the work and invoice. Taking steps at your request before a contract; our legitimate interest in answering an enquiry you sent.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td data-label="When">You book a call</td>
              <td data-label="What we receive">Name, email, the time, anything you write in the booking form. Held by Cal.com and the calendar provider.</td>
              <td data-label="Why">To hold the meeting. Taking steps at your request.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td data-label="When">You visit the site</td>
              <td data-label="What we receive">IP address and request details in the host's server logs</td>
              <td data-label="Why">To deliver the site and keep it secure. Legitimate interest. We do not read these logs ourselves.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>You do not have to give us anything to read the site or run the free check.</p>

        <h2>Who processes it for us</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>HubSpot</strong> stores brief submissions as contact records. We use the forms interface only and do not load HubSpot's tracking script on this site.</li>
          <li><strong>Google</strong> provides our email, calendar and the meeting link.</li>
          <li><strong>Cal.com</strong> handles booking. Its calendar loads <strong>only when you press "Load the calendar"</strong>; until then nothing is requested from Cal.com. Once loaded it may set its own cookies.</li>
          <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts the site and keeps the server logs described above.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These providers may process data outside your country, including in the United States, relying on the transfer safeguards the law provides. We do not sell or rent personal data.</p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>This site sets no cookies and loads no third-party fonts or tracking scripts. Fonts are served from the same site. The only third-party content you can load is the Cal.com calendar, and only by clicking.</p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Enquiries and bookings:</strong> up to 24 months after our last contact. If we work together, until the work and any follow-up end, then as long as the law requires for business records.</li>
          <li>We delete earlier if you ask.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on where you live, you can ask for a copy of your data, or ask us to correct it, delete it, restrict it, or move it. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will answer within one month. If you think we have handled your data badly you can complain to your local data protection authority; we would like the chance to put it right first.</p>

        <h2>Security and children</h2>
        <p>Data sits with the providers named above, which use encryption in transit and access controls. No system is perfectly secure, so we keep what we hold to the minimum above. The site is for business users and is not directed at anyone under 18.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>If this changes in a way that matters, the date at the top changes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
